      "note": [
        "The environmental accounts statistics on air emissions are calculated with a production perspective and cover direct emissions from Swedish economic actors, regardless of the geographical location of the emissions. The production perspective differs from the territorial perspective (used for emissions inventories as reported to the UNFCCC) which covers all emissions arising inside Sweden´s border. Much of the source data used to produce the environmental accounts statistics on air emissions are produced with a territorial perspective. In order to adjust for the difference between the environmental accounts production perspective and the territorial perspective of source data, a so-called residence adjustment is applied. It is applied primarily for transport-related emissions. More information about the calculation method and source data used for the residence adjustment is available in the quality declaration for the statistics (in Swedish only).",
        "2024-05-29: In connection with the publication on 29 May, the statistics for many Nace:s were revised in year 2022."
      ],
